# Redirect rules for Workers static assets. 301 unless noted.
#
# Only relative URLs are allowed here. Workers rejects a rule whose source or
# destination names a host, and rejects the whole file rather than the offending
# line: an absolute URL fails the deploy at version creation with
# "Invalid _redirects configuration ... [code: 100324]".
#
# This is the one place Pages and Workers diverge on this file. Pages accepted
# cross-host rules, which is how the apex-to-primary and secondary-domain
# redirects were written here originally. Those belong in Cloudflare Redirect
# Rules or Bulk Redirects at the zone level instead, configured once a domain
# exists. See docs/LAUNCH-CHECKLIST.md.
#
# Note that wrangler's dry run does not catch a bad rule. The file is validated
# server-side when the version is created, so the first sign of a mistake here
# is a failed deploy.

# Judge URLs are slugs, and slugs change when a name is corrected. Add a line
# here rather than breaking an inbound link from a mail piece already sent.
# /judges/old-slug/  /judges/new-slug/  301
